Expanding both quadratics yields $x^2+px+m = (x-r)(x-s)$ and $x^2+mx+n=(x-2r)(x-2s),$ so \[(x-r)(x-s) = \frac{1}{2}(x-2r)(x-2s),\] Dividing both sides by $2$ and expanding gives $mx+n=\frac{1}{2}(4rx+4sx-4r^2-4rs-4s^2).$ Therefore, \begin{align*}
m&=2rx+2sx-(2r^2+2rs+2s^2), \\
n&=-r^2-s^2.
\end{align*}

